# Marks who owns the paths where a change needs the maintainer's own eye. It does NOT require a review:
# the repository has one maintainer, who cannot approve their own pull request, so the main ruleset must keep
# "Require review from Code Owners" off. GitHub only lists the owner on a pull request that touches these paths.
# The last matching pattern decides.

# Branding, legal text and the screen that shows it.
/docs/branding/**               @yor42
/docs/Terms-of-Services.md      @yor42
/docs/Privacy-Policy.md         @yor42
/src/lib/Others/Legal.svelte    @yor42

# Signing material: none of it is tracked, so a match means something is being added that should not be.
/src-tauri/key.txt              @yor42
**/keystore*                    @yor42
**/keystore.properties          @yor42

# CI definitions run with repository permissions.
/.github/workflows/**           @yor42
/.github/scripts/**             @yor42
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @yor42
